From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Allen Zheng <zhenga8533@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] save: add KALEIDO_SAVE_MAGIC

With KALEIDO_SAVE_MAGIC defined, its value replaces the magic number in the save
footers (SAVE_MAGIC, for the main save and every extra save) and in the outside
data's block headers (SAVE_OUTSIDE_MAGIC, for the Mystery Gift cards and keys), so
that each game has its own.

A footer or header with another magic reads as never written, so a game finds no
save on a card of another game, Black 2's included: it offers New Game only, and a
new game takes none of that card's gifts or keys. The ROM header, and with it the
save type that emulators and flashcarts choose, doesn't change.
---
 src/ov331/save_outside.c | 6 ++++++
 src/system/save_table.c  | 7 ++++++-
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ov331/save_outside.c b/src/ov331/save_outside.c
index a550287e1..c191b3d30 100644
--- a/src/ov331/save_outside.c
+++ b/src/ov331/save_outside.c
@@ -17,7 +17,13 @@
 #define SAVE_OUTSIDE_SIZE 0xb00
 #define KEYS_SIZE 0x300
 
+// KALEIDO_SAVE_MAGIC too, so that a new game takes no gifts or keys from another game's card: a block with another
+// magic reads as never written
+#ifdef KALEIDO_SAVE_MAGIC
+#define SAVE_OUTSIDE_MAGIC KALEIDO_SAVE_MAGIC
+#else
 #define SAVE_OUTSIDE_MAGIC 0xa10f49ae
+#endif
 
 enum {
     BLOCK_GIFTS,
diff --git a/src/system/save_table.c b/src/system/save_table.c
index f5edd7e90..15bcc9057 100644
--- a/src/system/save_table.c
+++ b/src/system/save_table.c
@@ -55,11 +55,16 @@
 // name in the ROM; save_table.c is a guess. That it is a file apart from save_control.c shows in the order of its
 // tables, which MWCC only gives when the file defines nothing else.
 
-// Where the saves are on the card, and the magic number in their footers
+// Where the saves are on the card, and the magic number in their footers. KALEIDO_SAVE_MAGIC gives a game its own,
+// so that it finds no save on a card of another game: a footer with another magic reads as no save at all
 #define SAVE_MAIN_ADDR 0
 #define SAVE_BACKUP_ADDR 0x26000
 #define SAVE_SIZE 0x26000
+#ifdef KALEIDO_SAVE_MAGIC
+#define SAVE_MAGIC KALEIDO_SAVE_MAGIC
+#else
 #define SAVE_MAGIC 0x31053527
+#endif
 
 typedef void (*SaveBlockInit)(void *block);
 
